Kilowatt Country (kilowattcountry)

Inspired by Power Grid.

Game design, rules text, the map, the power plants, code and art: Luis Montes. The rules are restated in our own
words; the country, its cities and links (games/kilowattcountry/tools/gen-data.mjs, a seeded scatter and its
Gabriel graph) and the plant set (the same script, balance-checked against a worth line) are our own. Every
texture is drawn by games/kilowattcountry/tools/make-textures.mjs, the plant cards are painted in the game, and
the sounds are synthesised in code.

Built with cartwheel-engine and three.c (MIT). The font is the engine's built-in sans (see the engine's NOTICE).
The logo font is Fira Sans Bold (SIL Open Font Licence, shipped with the engine's samples).
